CORE
main.c
--no-standard-checks --refine-arithmetic
\[main\.assertion\.1\].*distributivity.*SUCCESS
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Tests bv_refinementt::detect_algebraic_pairs' distributivity branch:
mult(a, plus(b, c)) is recognised as equal to mult(a, b) + mult(a, c)
even when the outer mult result is laundered through an opaque
function call. Without this hint, the verification times out beyond
6-8 bits.
